    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0458" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/73</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-24T11:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 22, 7 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d396-f1"/> German ships, as previously
                    explained, have been seized and taken possession of by Government of Cuba. They
                    are prizes of war. There is no title of transference. President Menocal says
                    Cuban Government is not considering making money out of these ships and does not
                    care sell to shipping companies, if the United States wishes to use them it can
                    have them on any terms it wishes. If not he will have them used in trade between
                    United <pb facs="0459" n="287" xml:id="pg287"/> States and Cuba. He has offers
                    near quarter million dollars per month rental.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d396-f1" n="1" xml:id="d396-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram of Apr. 29, 1917, 11 a.m., to the Minister, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg270">p. 270</ref>.</p>
